  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math>  is more reactive in  <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow></msub><mn>2</mn></math>  reactions. In  <math><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math> , steric hindrance at the carbon of  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math>  is very high, therefore, the nucleophilic attack of phthalimide anion is mechanically hindered. <br/><br/>The  <math><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math>  and  <math><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math>  are electron-donating groups, which do not activate Br atom for nucleophilic substitutions reactions. Hence, compounds C and D are not also used for the preparation of amines.",
